-- title:
--   Compute one exterior-product array in singly exponential time
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbf v$ be a length-$d$ sign vector, with every entry equal to $1$ or $-1$, and let $A$ be an integer coefficient array of length $2^d$ whose entries have width at most $w$. Suppose the dimension counter contains $d$ markers and the recursive wedge scratch stacks are empty. The native later-array program consumes the framed accumulator $A$ and prepends the framed array
--   $$
--   \operatorname{wedgeReverse}(\mathbf v,A)
--   $$
--   to the current-output stack, preserving the label vector, dimension counter and all other saved data. The label components are supplied in reverse coordinate order; this operation implements the corresponding right exterior multiplication. The cost is at most
--   $$
--   10^6(d+2)^2(w+d+2)2^d.
--   $$
--   This is the array-level multiplication contract used in every later graph-DP cell.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/LaterArray.lean, line 16; source snapshot SHA-256 6c7f4db5d4b5ce298051c16d4ae5785f5849e3cd5a479cb6c82b8a4953acd2fd.

